docs/infra.md:50:**Signing in.** `/auth/login` redirects to the app's own form. The form posts the email to `/auth/email-code`, which hands it to Better Auth's verification-code endpoint, and Better Auth mails a six-digit code through the same `EmailSender` the invitations use. `/auth/email-code/verify` exchanges the code for a session: Better Auth writes the `auth_session` row, and its `Set-Cookie` value is put on our response as `__Host-surveybeat-session`. There is no callback route and no state cookie, because nothing redirects off-site, and there is no hosted logout page: sign-out deletes the session row and answers 303 to the app.
docs/infra.md:62:**Plugins.** `packages/auth/src/options.ts` enables Better Auth's `magicLink`, `admin`, `organization` and `passkey` plugins beside the email code (ADR 0024). A magic link is mailed through the same `EmailSender`, expires after 5 minutes and works once. The admin plugin's `role` is the auth plane's own, not the Organization admin (ADR 0003), and Organization creation stays the allowlisted flow, so the plugin's `auth_organization`, `auth_member` and `auth_invitation` rows are not the tenant. The passkey relying party comes from the stage's base URL. Plugin tables and columns are `d1-migrations/0009_better_auth_plugins.sql`.
docs/infra.md:78:The canary sweep therefore sends its canary 1000 times to each Worker (all lost with probability 0.99^1000 ≈ 4·10⁻⁵). It polls for up to 10 minutes until the Main Worker's canary is found (the positive control), then asserts that the Submission Worker produced zero events and that its canary is in no event. If logging were on, about 10 of its 1000 requests would be kept, so zero is meaningful. Checked on 2026-11-07 on a workers.dev stage: the sweep passed in 90 seconds (12 Main events found), and with the Submission Worker's logs switched on it failed (7 events, canary found).
